From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt Local Patch <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: avoid user-space fallback for optional
 firmware-N.bin

ath11k_fw_pre_init() requests the optional firmware-2.bin through
ath11k_core_firmware_request(), which uses firmware_request_nowarn().
When the file is absent and the firmware user-helper fallback is enabled,
the request can still trigger a user-space firmware request and wait for
the configured timeout before ath11k falls back to firmware API 1.

Use request_firmware_direct() for this optional API-N bundle lookup.
It checks the filesystem without invoking the user-space fallback loader.
The normal API 1 fallback remains unchanged.

This avoids the unnecessary firmware-loader timeout when firmware-2.bin
is not installed.

Based on the upstream ath11k patch:
https://lore.kernel.org/ath11k/20261101-b123-fw-api-n-direct-v1-1-a9b734520abc@gmail.com/

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Local Patch <noreply@example.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
index ef1b4c81843a3..3628e33e57f6e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
@@ -16,10 +16,14 @@ static int ath11k_fw_request_firmware_api_n(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	struct ath11k_fw_ie *hdr;
 	const u8 *data;
 	__le32 *timestamp;
-
-	ab->fw.fw = ath11k_core_firmware_request(ab, name);
-	if (IS_ERR(ab->fw.fw)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(ab->fw.fw);
+	char path[100];
+
+	/* The file is optional: look for it on the filesystem only, so a
+	 * missing one does not go through the user-space fallback loader.
+	 */
+	ath11k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, name, path, sizeof(path));
+	ret = request_firmware_direct(&ab->fw.fw, path, ab->dev);
+	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_BOOT, "failed to load %s: %d\n", name, ret);
 		ab->fw.fw = NULL;
 		return ret;
-- 
